From a4013f7991defc843ec0e685811bd5dfbf4bc7ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:22:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: software full-disk encryption for the opt-in, no
 Qualcomm HW FDE

TARGET_HW_DISK_ENCRYPTION (stock Android 7's Qualcomm hardware disk
encryption, libcryptfs_hw) built vold against the cryptfshw HAL, which
this port does not have: Settings' "Encrypt tablet" stopped with
"Failed to get Cryptfshw service" and left its convert_fde breadcrumb,
so every boot retried and rebooted. Encryption stays off by default;
the opt-in now uses vold's software dm-crypt (CPU AES instructions, the
key bound to the TrustZone keymaster).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 board/crypto.mk | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/board/crypto.mk b/board/crypto.mk
index 31c9e69..d35d132 100644
--- a/board/crypto.mk
+++ b/board/crypto.mk
@@ -1,2 +1,5 @@
-# Encryption
-TARGET_HW_DISK_ENCRYPTION := true
+# Encryption: off by default (fstab encryptable=footer), with Settings' "Encrypt tablet" as the
+# opt-in. That runs vold's software full-disk encryption (dm-crypt with the CPU's AES
+# instructions; the key protected by the TrustZone keymaster). TARGET_HW_DISK_ENCRYPTION is not
+# set: Qualcomm's hardware disk encryption (stock Android 7's, libcryptfs_hw) needs the cryptfshw
+# HAL, which this port does not have, and vold refused to encrypt without it.
-- 
2.53.0

